/*!
\ingroup qmllint-warnings-and-errors

\title Max warnings exceeded
\brief [max-warnings-exceeded] A regression on qmllint warnings was detected.

\qmllintwarningcategory max-warnings-exceeded

\section1 Amount of warnings exceeded the limit set by MaxWarnings

\section2 What happened?
The number of qmllint warnings on a QML file exceeded the threshold set via the
\c MaxWarnings value in the \l {qmllint#Settings}{qmllint settings file}.

\section2 Why is that bad?
\c MaxWarnings can be set to control or forbid the introduction of non-clean QML
code to ensure a certain level of QML code quality. Introducing new qmllint
warnings in a project decreases the code quality of the project.

To fix this warning,
\list
\li Fix the new warnings to decrease the number of total warnings back to the
    configured threshold.
\li Increase the number of allowed max warnings via the \l {qmllint#Settings}
    {qmllint settings file} if fixing the new warnings is not feasible.
\endlist

*/
